+[Term]
+id: MONDO:7770003
+name: HMBS-related hepatic porphyria
+def: "A hepatic porphyria caused by monoallelic or biallelic variants in HMBS and presenting as a spectrum of disease with a semidominant inheritance pattern. Monoallelic variants predispose to acute or episodic attacks in adulthood with abdominal pain, neuropathy, and neuropsychiatric symptoms without cutaneous manifestations. Triggers precipitating acute attacks include estrogen or progesterone, oral contraceptives, alcohol, drugs, stress, or infections. Biallelic variants cause severe disease in childhood, presenting with neurological issues including developmental abnormalities, ataxia, dysarthria, leukoencephalopathy, cataracts, and optic nerve hypoplasia." [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40097/, https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9703]
+subset: clingen {source="MONDO:CLINGEN"}
+subset: rare
+is_a: MONDO:0002520 {source="https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40097/"} ! hepatic porphyria
+is_a: MONDO:0019142 {source="https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40097/"} ! inherited porphyria
