+[Term]
+id: MONDO:7770005
+name: PPOX-related hepatic porphyria
+def: "A hepatic porphyria caused by monoallelic or biallelic variants in PPOX and presenting as a spectrum of disease with a semidominant inheritance pattern. Cases caused by monoallelic variants may have adolescent or adult onset and are episodic, characterized by abdominal pain, constipation, vomiting, muscular paralysis, and psychosis; other symptoms may include abnormal blistering of the skin, cutaneous photosensitivity, and neuropathy. Triggers precipitating acute attacks include estrogen or progesterone, oral contraceptives, alcohol, drugs, stress, or infections. Cases caused by biallelic variants, which reduce enzyme activity to less than 25% of normal, typically result in child or adolescent onset with greater severity and may include brachydactyly, clinodactyly, intellectual disability, nystagmus, myopia, growth retardation, and hyperpigmentation." [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40097/, https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9703]
+subset: clingen {source="MONDO:CLINGEN"}
+subset: rare
+is_a: MONDO:0002520 {source="https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40097/"} ! hepatic porphyria
+is_a: MONDO:0019142 {source="https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40097/"} ! inherited porphyria
+intersection_of: MONDO:0002520 ! hepatic porphyria
